{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "lambda(1) = 1 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)\n  how: 1 = 1; lambda is the lcm of nothing: 1\n  lambda(2^e) = 2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(1) = 1\n  check: the lcm of the orders of all units, by stepping through their powers: 1\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "carmichael", "ucas": "carmichael 1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "carmichael", "method": "1 = 1; lambda is the lcm of nothing: 1", "lambda(2^e)": "2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(1) = 1", "headline": "lambda(1) = 1 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the lcm of the orders of all units, by stepping through their powers: 1"}], "files": [], "text": "lambda(1) = 1 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)\n  how: 1 = 1; lambda is the lcm of nothing: 1\n  lambda(2^e) = 2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(1) = 1\n  check: the lcm of the orders of all units, by stepping through their powers: 1\n"}, "isError": false}}
