{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 30, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "3^-1 = 4 mod 11\n  how: extended Euclid: 4*3 - 1*11 = 1\n  check: 3 * 4 = 12 = 1*11 + 1\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 30, "ok": true, "cmd": "inverse_mod", "ucas": "inverse 3 mod 11", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "inverse", "method": "extended Euclid: 4*3 - 1*11 = 1", "lhs": "3^-1", "modulus": "11", "value": "4", "value_int": 4, "headline": "3^-1 = 4 mod 11"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "3 * 4 = 12 = 1*11 + 1"}], "files": [], "text": "3^-1 = 4 mod 11\n  how: extended Euclid: 4*3 - 1*11 = 1\n  check: 3 * 4 = 12 = 1*11 + 1\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 31, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "2 has no inverse mod 4: gcd(2, 4) = 2 > 1\n  2 * 2 = 4 = 0 mod 4, so 2 is a zero divisor; a*x = 1 would give 2 = 2 * 2 * x = 0\n  the units mod 4 are the residues coprime to 4 (phi(4) = 2 of them)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 31, "ok": true, "cmd": "inverse_mod", "ucas": "inverse 2 mod 4", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "inverse", "headline": "2 has no inverse mod 4: gcd(2, 4) = 2 > 1", "details": ["2 * 2 = 4 = 0 mod 4, so 2 is a zero divisor; a*x = 1 would give 2 = 2 * 2 * x = 0", "the units mod 4 are the residues coprime to 4 (phi(4) = 2 of them)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "2 has no inverse mod 4: gcd(2, 4) = 2 > 1\n  2 * 2 = 4 = 0 mod 4, so 2 is a zero divisor; a*x = 1 would give 2 = 2 * 2 * x = 0\n  the units mod 4 are the residues coprime to 4 (phi(4) = 2 of them)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 32, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "ord(3) = 5 mod 11\n  how: the order divides lambda(11) = 10; 3^5 = 1 and 3^(5/5) = 3\n  not a primitive root: phi(11) = 10\n  additive order: 11\n  check: stepping through the powers, 3^k = 1 first at k = 5\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 32, "ok": true, "cmd": "order_mod", "ucas": "order 3 mod 11", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "order", "method": "the order divides lambda(11) = 10; 3^5 = 1 and 3^(5/5) = 3", "not_a_primitive_root": "phi(11) = 10", "additive_order": "11", "lhs": "ord(3)", "modulus": "11", "value": "5", "value_int": 5, "headline": "ord(3) = 5 mod 11"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "stepping through the powers, 3^k = 1 first at k = 5"}], "files": [], "text": "ord(3) = 5 mod 11\n  how: the order divides lambda(11) = 10; 3^5 = 1 and 3^(5/5) = 3\n  not a primitive root: phi(11) = 10\n  additive order: 11\n  check: stepping through the powers, 3^k = 1 first at k = 5\n"}, "isError": false}}
